---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ResumeButton from "../components/ResumeButton.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About — Dylan Coon" description="About me, my skills, and what I'm working on.">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 relative">
    <!-- Background glow -->
    <div class="absolute -top-10 -left-20 w-72 h-72 bg-[var(--color-accent)]/6 rounded-full blur-3xl pointer-events-none"></div>

    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-3 tracking-tight">About Me</h1>
    <p class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] mb-6">
      Software engineer, problem solver, outdoor enthusiast.
    </p>

    <!-- Divider -->
    <div class="h-px bg-gradient-to-r from-[var(--color-accent)]/30 via-[var(--color-border)] to-transparent mb-12"></div>

    <div class="prose mb-14">
      <p>
        Hi! My name is Dylan Coon and I am from Erie, Pennsylvania. I'm a software engineer
        with a strong foundation in computer science and a passion for solving complex problems.
        I graduated from Penn State University with a degree in Computer Science and a minor in
        Mathematics, where I built a deep understanding of algorithms, systems, and logical
        thinking — skills I apply daily in my work and personal projects. I work mostly in
        Python, Go, C++, and C, and I'm familiar with JavaScript and TypeScript. I have worked
        with GCP quite a bit as well as AWS on occasion. I am always eager to learn new
        languages and tools.
      </p>

      <p>
        I started my career as an intern at Iron Mountain — an information management company
        known for their cloud based solutions they provide to hundreds of clients globally. As
        an intern, I worked on a ML team that specialized in model optimization and refactoring
        for intelligent document processing. I wrote Python code to extract signatures from
        documents and structure training data in a concurrent manner using a threading library.
        Today I'm a software engineer at the company on an application support team, where
        much of my work is reliability engineering: I monitor our cloud environments on GCP,
        collect metrics on system health, build Python automation that replaces manual
        operational work, and validate new releases in production. That work is what pulled me
        toward infrastructure and SRE, and it's where I want to keep growing.
      </p>

      <p>
        Outside of work, my projects focus on running ML systems reliably. I built an
        <a href="/projects/gaze-evaluation-platform">evaluation platform for gaze models</a>
        where every model is evaluated in a container, logged to MLflow, and gated in CI, so a
        merge is blocked if any metric regresses. I also built a
        <a href="/projects/realtime-detection-pipeline">real-time object detection pipeline</a>
        on a Raspberry Pi 5: YOLOv8 inference in C++, detection events streamed through Kafka,
        live data in Redis, history in PostgreSQL, and a React dashboard on top. Earlier
        projects like a CHIP-8 emulator in C++ and a key-value store in Go are where I got
        comfortable with systems programming.
      </p>

      <p>
        I'm also into robotics, and lately drones. I built an auto-tracking camera gimbal using
        a Raspberry Pi and OpenCV, and I'm currently working on a 3-axis robotic arm with
        stepper motors and 3D-printed links — implementing forward and inverse kinematics from
        scratch. My newest track is drone autonomy:
        <a href="/projects/gridplan">Gridplan</a>, a C++/Python path-planning library, is the
        first piece, with trajectory generation and real-time replanning to follow. I enjoy the
        overlap between software and hardware, especially when it involves control systems and
        real-time feedback loops.
      </p>

      <p>
        When I'm away from a screen, I like to be outside and spend time with my dog Yankee.
        I am also an avid rock climber — I love the mental and physical puzzle that each climb
        presents. It's a great complement to my love of problem-solving in software.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mb-14">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-5">Skills</h2>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="glow-card rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface)] p-5">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-accent-light)] mb-1.5">Languages</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Python, Go, C++, C</p>
        </div>
        <div class="glow-card rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface)] p-5">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-accent-light)] mb-1.5">Cloud</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">GCP, AWS</p>
        </div>
        <div class="glow-card rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface)] p-5 sm:col-span-2">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-accent-light)] mb-1.5">Infrastructure &amp; Tooling</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Docker, GitHub Actions, Kafka, Redis, PostgreSQL, MLflow, DVC, FastAPI, ONNX Runtime</p>
        </div>
        <div class="glow-card rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface)] p-5">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-accent-light)] mb-1.5">Interests</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Infrastructure, SRE, DevOps, ML systems, robotics and autonomy</p>
        </div>
        <div class="glow-card rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface)] p-5">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-accent-light)] mb-1.5">Education</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Penn State University — B.S. Computer Science, Minor in Mathematics</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mb-14">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-3">This Site</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Built with <a href="https://astro.build" class="text-[var(--color-accent-light)] hover:underline">Astro</a> and
        <a href="https://tailwindcss.com" class="text-[var(--color-accent-light)] hover:underline">Tailwind CSS</a>.
        Deployed on Cloudflare Pages. Content authored in Markdown.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="flex gap-3">
      <a
        href="https://github.com/DylanCoon99"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
        class="github-btn"
      >
        <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M8 0C3.58 0 0 3.58 0 8c0 3.54 2.29 6.53 5.47 7.59.4.07.55-.17.55-.38 0-.19-.01-.82-.01-1.49-2.01.37-2.53-.49-2.69-.94-.09-.23-.48-.94-.82-1.13-.28-.15-.68-.52-.01-.53.63-.01 1.08.58 1.23.82.72 1.21 1.87.87 2.33.66.07-.52.28-.87.51-1.07-1.78-.2-3.64-.89-3.64-3.95 0-.87.31-1.59.82-2.15-.08-.2-.36-1.02.08-2.12 0 0 .67-.21 2.2.82.64-.18 1.32-.27 2-.27.68 0 1.36.09 2 .27 1.53-1.04 2.2-.82 2.2-.82.44 1.1.16 1.92.08 2.12.51.56.82 1.27.82 2.15 0 3.07-1.87 3.75-3.65 3.95.29.25.54.73.54 1.48 0 1.07-.01 1.93-.01 2.2 0 .21.15.46.55.38A8.013 8.013 0 0016 8c0-4.42-3.58-8-8-8z"/>
        </svg>
        GitHub
      </a>
      <a
        href="mailto:dylcoon99@gmail.com"
        class="px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium border border-[var(--color-border)] text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] bg-[var(--color-surface)] hover:border-[var(--color-accent)]/40 hover:text-[var(--color-text)] hover:shadow-[0_0_20px_var(--color-accent-glow)] transition-all"
      >
        Email
      </a>
      <ResumeButton class="px-5 py-2.5" />
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
